{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-k2-reviewer-fable-50","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:47cd49c1ecba9907e7a1","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow aggregates each reactor's five weekly yield records to a single mean before any test: summarise_reactors buckets rows by reactor_id and computes mean(bucket['yields']) as one ReactorSummary per reactor.","observed_value":"12 ReactorSummary objects, one mean_yield each, from 60 weekly rows","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":66,"end_line":73,"quoted_text":"summaries.append(\n            ReactorSummary(\n                reactor_id=reactor,\n                pretreatment=bucket[\"pretreatment\"],\n                n_weeks=len(bucket[\"yields\"]),\n                mean_yield=mean(bucket[\"yields\"]),\n            )\n        )"}]},{"description":"The Mann-Whitney U test is applied only to the reactor-level means, not to the 60 weekly rows: the reference and treatment lists are comprehensions over the 12 summaries, and those lists are passed to mannwhitneyu.","observed_value":"6 control means vs 6 alkaline means passed to mannwhitneyu","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":173,"end_line":178,"quoted_text":"reference = [item.mean_yield for item in summaries if item.pretreatment == REFERENCE]\n    treatment = [item.mean_yield for item in summaries if item.pretreatment == TREATMENT]\n    if not reference or not treatment:\n        raise ValueError(\"both pretreatment groups must be present\")\n\n    outcome = mannwhitneyu(treatment, reference, alternative=\"two-sided\", method=\"exact\")"}]},{"description":"The reported test statistics are numerically consistent with exactly one value per reactor entering the test. Hand-recomputation of U from the 12 reactor means in the report's own table gives U = 4+5+6+6+6+6 = 33 (pairs where an alkaline mean exceeds a control mean), the maximum possible U for 6 vs 6 units is 36, rank-biserial = 2*33/36 - 1 = 0.833, and the exact two-sided p for U=33 with n1=n2=6 is 14/924 = 0.01515, matching the reported p = 0.0152. If the 60 weekly rows had entered the test, U could range up to 30*30 = 900 and these values would be impossible.","observed_value":"U = 33.0 of max 36, p = 0.0152 = 14/924, rank-biserial = 0.833","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":39,"end_line":39,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Two-sided exact Mann-Whitney U test on 12 reactor-level mean methane yields (6 control vs 6 alkaline reactors, one value per reactor): U = 33.0, p = 0.0152, rank-biserial correlation = 0.833; alkaline-pretreated reactors reached a higher steady-state yield (median 262.20 vs 215.90 NL CH4 per g VS, difference in group means 40.00 NL/g VS)."}]},{"description":"The reactor-level means reported in the summary table are correct aggregations of the raw weekly rows; e.g., R01's five weekly yields (199.1, 190.2, 205.4, 195.5, 202.8) average to 198.60 as reported, confirming the analysed values are per-reactor summaries of the raw file.","observed_value":"(199.1+190.2+205.4+195.5+202.8)/5 = 198.60","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"R01,control,4,2.08,7.42,199.1\nR01,control,5,2.11,7.38,190.2\nR01,control,6,2.09,7.45,205.4\nR01,control,7,2.12,7.41,195.5\nR01,control,8,2.10,7.44,202.8"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15,"quoted_text":"| R01 | control | 5 | 198.60 |"}]},{"description":"The report's stated sample size for the claim matches the independent-unit structure declared in the data description (independent unit = reactor_id), and the report explicitly disclaims using the 60 weekly rows as sample size.","observed_value":"claimed n = 12 reactors (6 vs 6), not 60 rows","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"One row is: one weekly monitoring record for a single pilot digester in a single run week\nIndependent unit column: reactor_id"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":41,"end_line":41,"quoted_text":"The comparison is made at the reactor level because pretreatment was applied to reactors, not to weekly samples; the 60 weekly records support the reactor means but do not enlarge the sample size for this claim."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The raw input file does contain repeated rows per independent unit (5 weekly rows for each of the 12 reactors, 60 rows total), so the precondition for the issue class exists in the data; the question was whether these repeated rows entered the row-independent test directly. They do not, but this structural feature is the strongest potential trigger and is noted as counterevidence considered.","observed_value":"60 rows = 12 reactors x 5 weeks in long format","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"reactor_id,pretreatment,run_week,olr_g_vs_per_l_d,digestate_ph,ch4_yield_nl_per_g_vs\nR01,control,4,2.08,7.42,199.1\nR01,control,5,2.11,7.38,190.2\nR01,control,6,2.09,7.45,205.4\nR01,control,7,2.12,7.41,195.5\nR01,control,8,2.10,7.44,202.8"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":23,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"A digester therefore contributes five rows to the file but only one independent value to any comparison between the two pretreatments; the weekly records serve to estimate that reactor's steady-state level, not to increase the number of units."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to show that the 60 weekly rows entered the Mann-Whitney test directly. First, I traced the code path: mannwhitneyu receives lists built from the 12 ReactorSummary.mean_yield values, not from raw rows, and summarise_reactors raises on inconsistent pretreatment labels or duplicated weeks within a reactor. Second, I checked the reported statistics for row-level leakage: with 30 vs 30 weekly rows the maximum U would be 900, but the reported U = 33.0 lies within the 6x6 unit-level maximum of 36; recomputing U by hand from the 12 reactor means gives exactly 33, rank-biserial 2*33/36-1 = 0.833 matches, and the exact two-sided p for n1=n2=6 at U=33 is 2*7/924 = 0.01515, matching the reported 0.0152. Third, I recomputed all 12 reactor means and both group summaries (control mean 220.00, alkaline mean 260.00, medians 215.90 and 262.20) from the raw CSV and they match the report. Every check failed to demonstrate the issue; the analysis consumes exactly one value per independent reactor.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}